Hey Ozias,

Raster::extract returns a list when given a spatialPolygons object (see 'value' section in https://www.rdocumentation.org/packages/raster/versions/2.6-7/topics/extract). I'd run through the code without looping first to see if that is the output you want. Otherwise you may be looking for the raster::mask function instead.

Also the R-Sig-geo listserve is a good way to get spatial questions answered quickly.

Best,

Steve

