Hi

Yes, with extract, you are returning a list (or data.frame with df=TRUE). But note that extract is meant usually to do shape-wise statistics (compute mean for every country, etc). I suspect in your case what you mean by "extract" is covered by the crop() function: https://www.rdocumentation.org/packages/raster/versions/2.6-7/topics/crop

Note that the crop function can write directly the raster! This should save you a lot of effort (and lot of on-cache disk writing). The ... argument in crop() refer to arguments in writeRaster directly!

Best,

Matthieu

